        "original_id": "a796bb39-0d84-5c58-8bfb-ced438a16ead",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Tropicana Products, PepsiCo, Pepsi-Cola company\n- People: Anthony T. Rossi\n- Products: Mountain Dew\n- Places: Bradenton, Florida, United States, Canada\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony Talamo Rossi was born on September 13, 1900, and died on January 24, 1993.\n- Anthony Talamo Rossi was an Italian immigrant who founded Tropicana Products in 1947 in Bradenton, Florida, in the United States.\n- Tropicana Products was founded as a producer of orange juice.\n- In August 1964, the Pepsi-Cola company acquired the Mountain Dew brand and production rights from Tip.\n- After the August 1964 acquisition, Mountain Dew distribution expanded more widely across the United States and Canada.\n- Since 1998, Tropicana Products has been owned by PepsiCo.\n- By 2004, Tropicana Products had grown from 50 employees to over 8,000 employees.\n- By 2004, Tropicana Products had expanded into multiple product lines and had become one of the world's largest producers and marketers of citrus juice.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
